\mainpage tapi

\tableofcontents

\section description Description

`tapi` is a small C testing framework focused on simple test
definitions, runtime-based mocking, clear assertions, and quick integration into existing projects.
The idea for the framework stemmed from a personal need to write unit tests for some programs that
were written in C. When looking for a stable testing framework, it became prevalent that none of the
existing options were quite what was needed (*like GoogleTest,
CMock, CMocka*). These frameworks were either too heavyweight or implemented mocking in a
significantly more complicated way. The goal with this framework is to provide a simple,
easy-to-use, cross-platform testing framework that can be integrated into existing projects, with a
very simple form of mocking (*stub and patch*). If you want to learn more about the design of the
framework, you can read more about \ref mocking "mocking, patching" here.

